  "body": "From the fifth review of PR #135 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/135#issuecomment-6713905271). `CreateOperation` never sets an explicit order, so ops with no order sort by name in the program. That holds for ops made in the GUI too: an op named 'Finish' posts before one named 'Rough' in the same setup, whatever order the user created them in or the tree shows.\n\nSince #103 and #109, the turning and prior laws read the ops ahead in program order, so this order now decides verdicts. The finish runs on raw bar and is convicted, which is safe (it fails closed) but surprising. The deeper problem is that the posted order differs from what the user sees.\n\nDone means: CreateOperation appends the op at the end of its setup's program order (an explicit order index), the tree and the post agree, and old projects with no order keep their current name order on load (no silent reorder of existing programs). Pin: create Rough then Finish and check the program order is Rough, Finish; create 'B' then 'A' and check it is B, A.",
